1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,261
Module ten: flexible endoscope

2
00:00:06,261 --> 00:00:09,714
reprocessing. Here is the whole device,

3
00:00:09,714 --> 00:00:12,009
from control body to insertion tube to

4
00:00:12,009 --> 00:00:15,121
distal tip. It is semi-critical,

5
00:00:15,121 --> 00:00:17,689
heat-labile, mechanically complex, and the

6
00:00:17,689 --> 00:00:19,825
source of the most serious documented

7
00:00:19,825 --> 00:00:20,741
outbreaks.

8
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:25,731
Cut across the insertion tube and you see

9
00:00:25,731 --> 00:00:27,640
why these devices are mechanically

10
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,984
complex. Inside the sheath run several

11
00:00:30,984 --> 00:00:33,132
narrow channels of different diameters:

12
00:00:33,132 --> 00:00:35,359
the suction or biopsy channel, the air

13
00:00:35,359 --> 00:00:37,252
channel, and the water channel.

14
00:00:38,091 --> 00:00:40,614
Some are difficult to access, and some are

15
00:00:40,614 --> 00:00:43,742
easy to forget. These channels run the

16
00:00:43,742 --> 00:00:46,037
whole length of the scope, so every one of

17
00:00:46,037 --> 00:00:48,203
them must be reached during cleaning.

18
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:52,624
Heat is the first difference.

19
00:00:53,479 --> 00:00:56,093
Flexible endoscopes are heat-labile, so

20
00:00:56,093 --> 00:00:58,099
they cannot be steam sterilised.

21
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,956
High-level disinfection is the usual

22
00:01:00,956 --> 00:01:03,410
process, and it has a smaller margin than

23
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:06,452
sterilisation. They are also heavily

24
00:01:06,452 --> 00:01:09,247
contaminated in use, with organic material

25
00:01:09,247 --> 00:01:10,947
and a high bacterial load.

26
00:01:11,809 --> 00:01:14,218
And they are expensive, so hospitals own

27
00:01:14,218 --> 00:01:16,229
few and there is constant pressure on

28
00:01:16,229 --> 00:01:17,407
turnaround time.

29
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:22,188
The sequence starts at the bedside,

30
00:01:22,203 --> 00:01:24,556
immediately after the procedure and before

31
00:01:24,556 --> 00:01:25,983
the scope leaves the room.

32
00:01:26,831 --> 00:01:29,149
Wipe the insertion tube and suction or

33
00:01:29,149 --> 00:01:30,797
flush the channels with the agreed

34
00:01:30,797 --> 00:01:34,409
solution. Organic material begins to dry

35
00:01:34,409 --> 00:01:36,738
and to form biofilm within minutes, and

36
00:01:36,738 --> 00:01:39,386
once it has, no subsequent step reliably

37
00:01:39,386 --> 00:01:42,633
removes it. This is the step performed by

38
00:01:42,633 --> 00:01:45,019
the busiest person at the busiest moment,

39
00:01:45,019 --> 00:01:47,481
and it is the one most often abbreviated.

40
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:52,611
Before immersion, every time, without

41
00:01:52,611 --> 00:01:55,016
exception, the scope is pressurised.

42
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:57,980
Bubbles escaping show a breach in the

43
00:01:57,980 --> 00:02:00,384
outer sheath, and the pressure falls.

44
00:02:01,224 --> 00:02:04,072
Scopes are fragile, so damage is common.

45
00:02:04,902 --> 00:02:07,436
An immersed, damaged scope admits fluid

46
00:02:07,436 --> 00:02:09,447
into its interior, where it cannot be

47
00:02:09,447 --> 00:02:11,697
cleaned or disinfected and organisms

48
00:02:11,697 --> 00:02:14,734
multiply. It is then contaminated

49
00:02:14,734 --> 00:02:16,927
internally and irreparably, and will be

50
00:02:16,927 --> 00:02:19,393
used on patients until the damage is found

51
00:02:19,393 --> 00:02:22,681
by other means. The test takes a minute,

52
00:02:22,681 --> 00:02:24,363
and is skipped when the list is running

53
00:02:24,363 --> 00:02:24,926
late.

54
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:29,097
Look at the channel wall.

55
00:02:29,925 --> 00:02:32,391
Biofilm forms readily there, and once

56
00:02:32,391 --> 00:02:34,095
established it resists chemical

57
00:02:34,095 --> 00:02:35,784
disinfection entirely.

58
00:02:36,699 --> 00:02:39,358
Disinfectant alone cannot clear it, which

59
00:02:39,358 --> 00:02:41,819
is why manual cleaning is irreplaceable.

60
00:02:42,657 --> 00:02:44,884
The brush must be of the correct diameter

61
00:02:44,884 --> 00:02:46,941
and length for that specific model,

62
00:02:46,941 --> 00:02:49,437
following the manufacturer's instructions.

63
00:02:50,271 --> 00:02:52,339
It is passed through every channel until

64
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,771
it emerges visibly clean, and brushing is

65
00:02:54,771 --> 00:02:56,437
repeated until it does.

66
00:02:57,285 --> 00:02:59,137
Two scopes that look similar may have

67
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,944
different channels, connectors and

68
00:03:00,944 --> 00:03:01,940
instructions.

69
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,509
Here is the sequence through manual

70
00:03:06,509 --> 00:03:10,142
cleaning. Bedside pre-clean comes first,

71
00:03:10,142 --> 00:03:11,421
then the leak test.

72
00:03:12,268 --> 00:03:13,768
Then immerse fully in the correct

73
00:03:13,768 --> 00:03:15,745
detergent at the correct dilution and

74
00:03:15,745 --> 00:03:17,973
temperature, and wipe the exterior and

75
00:03:17,973 --> 00:03:21,696
insertion tube. Brush every channel, plus

76
00:03:21,696 --> 00:03:24,340
ports, valves and the elevator recess.

77
00:03:25,168 --> 00:03:27,429
Flush all channels with detergent, then

78
00:03:27,429 --> 00:03:29,941
water, using the connectors specified for

79
00:03:29,941 --> 00:03:33,803
that model. Remove, clean and disinfect or

80
00:03:33,803 --> 00:03:36,314
replace valves, buttons and caps, which

81
00:03:36,314 --> 00:03:37,833
are frequently forgotten.

82
00:03:38,668 --> 00:03:41,236
Finally, inspect for damage and residual

83
00:03:41,236 --> 00:03:41,857
soil.

84
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:48,067
To summarise. Flexible endoscopes are

85
00:03:48,067 --> 00:03:50,647
heat-labile, mechanically complex, heavily

86
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:53,204
soiled, expensive and fragile, which is

87
00:03:53,204 --> 00:03:55,181
why they have caused several of the most

88
00:03:55,181 --> 00:03:57,290
serious documented outbreaks.

89
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,359
Pre-clean at the bedside within minutes,

90
00:04:00,359 --> 00:04:02,911
because biofilm resists later steps.

91
00:04:03,742 --> 00:04:06,401
Leak test before every immersion, without

92
00:04:06,401 --> 00:04:10,001
exception. Then clean manually, brushing

93
00:04:10,001 --> 00:04:12,160
every channel until the brush emerges

94
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:15,337
visibly clean. Next, we look at the

95
00:04:15,337 --> 00:04:17,871
duodenoscope elevator, and at drying and

96
00:04:17,871 --> 00:04:18,628
storage.

97
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:23,035
Keep learning with MedSkills.

